				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Correct Terminal RPC method naming to match Vine proto\n\nUpdate the gRPC request string for terminal creation in `Services/Terminal/Service.ts` from `\"terminal.create\"` to `\"$terminal:create\"`. This aligns the invocation with the exact PascalCase and namespace-prefixed definition in the `Vine.proto` specification.\n\nThe previous lowercase dot-notation format is inconsistent with the strongly-typed IPC contract established for the Mountain backend, potentially causing method resolution failures. This change ensures the `Create` operation is correctly routed to the terminal handler in the extension host.\n\nImpact: Restores reliable terminal instance creation via the gRPC bridge.",
			"SHA": "d6c9004c8f04387f4a4ca37e1aea56a262e681f5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:25:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				5
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Robust URI string reconstruction in gRPC handlers\n\nReplace fragile reliance on `.toString()` and `.external` properties with explicit structural checks across Document, Language, Notification, Window, and gRPC handlers. When a Uri object lacks standard string conversion, construct the URL manually using `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties.\n\nThis prevents malformed URIs from being sent to Mountain during RPC calls, ensuring robust request routing for file operations and document events even when VS Code's URI implementation varies or shim interactions fail.\n\nImpact: Restores stability in file access, language provider invocations, and notification flows by guaranteeing valid URI strings are transmitted over the gRPC wire.",
			"SHA": "217fc9329f143b6057295e361d30dfcf4ecda7aa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T09:20:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				52
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Introduce Storage.GetItems method and refine URI resolution\n\nAdd `Storage.GetItems` to the Mountain RPC method set in `RouteManifest.ts`, increasing the known method count to 137. This expands the storage interface beyond simple key-value pairs to support bulk retrieval, aligning with the `Vine.proto` contract.\n\nRefactor the URI parsing logic in `Services/Handler/Request/Routing/Handler.ts` to robustly construct URL strings from `Uri` objects. The previous implementation relied on `.toString()` or `.external` properties; the new logic explicitly checks for `scheme`, `authority`, and `path` properties to construct `scheme://authority/path` when standard string conversion fails, preventing malformed URIs during request routing.\n\nAll ESBuild artifacts and the RouteManifest report are regenerated to reflect these source changes.",
			"SHA": "e9951a8909034edfe9cae2eb20308c3ce1353eba"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T07:59:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				43
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Align RPC method names with Vine proto PascalCase\n\nUpdate the gRPC method invocation strings across multiple Cocoon services to match the exact PascalCase naming defined in the `Vine.proto` specification. Replace legacy camelCase and lowercase prefixes (e.g., `window.showMessage`, `fs.stat`, `storage:set`) with their canonical counterparts (`Window.ShowMessage`, `FileSystem.Stat`, `Storage.GetItems`).\n\nApply corrections in the following namespaces:\n- `API/Factory`: Map VS Code message dialogs to `Window.ShowMessage`.\n- `Extension/Context`: Align memento storage calls to `Storage.GetItems` and `Storage.Set`.\n- `File/Service`: Standardize file system operations (`FileSystem.Stat`, `ReadFile`, `WriteFile`, `ReadDirectory`, `CreateDirectory`, `Delete`, `Rename`).\n- `Tasks`: Rename `taskType` to `type` in provider registration payloads.\n- `Workspace/Text/Document`: Switch `saveAll` fallback from notification to `Workspace.SaveAll` request to bypass silent Tauri re-emission issues.\n- `Terminal`: Correct send text to `$terminal:sendText`.\n\nThis ensures strict adherence to the strongly-typed IPC contract, preventing silent failures where the Mountain backend rejects unrecognized method names during the gRPC call resolution phase.",
			"SHA": "4cfa806fcad082e2acd24678913c01bb5078a0f7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T07:05:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1181,
				38
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Include file selector metadata in custom editor registration\n\nEnhance the `RegisterCustomEditor` handler in the Window namespace to scan the `Context.ExtensionRegistry` for the custom editor contribution matching the `ViewType`. Extract the file `Selector` (glob patterns like `*.{png,jpg}`) and include it in the payload sent to Mountain via `webview.registerCustomEditor`.\n\nPreviously, only the `ViewType` and `Options` were transmitted. Without the selector, Mountain lacks the necessary context to register the editor with `IEditorResolverService`, preventing VS Code from routing file opens to the custom editor instead of the default text editor.\n\nThis change ensures the full registration contract is satisfied, allowing custom editors defined in `package.json` to be correctly activated and file associations to be honored. The commit also includes a standard regeneration of the `RouteManifest` timestamp and all ESBuild artifacts in the `Target/` directory.",
			"SHA": "c3faa474ad2232dc1b76d66fb046deec30ef8a57"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781883342269
}